> directed by Peter Weir.

I just saw it over the weekend, and I think Tim is right.... definitely 
worth seeing.  It has strong Extropian appeal, because of the theme of 
overcoming death, and how that experience can alienate someone from others 
who have not been through it.  Unlike one reviewer I read, I didn't think 
it was up to the standards of Weir's "The Year of Living Dangerously" -- I 
found it a bit cliche towards the middle -- but still a damn good film.  
This is the only movie I've seen recently where no one in the audience 
talked after the first five minutes -- it was that powerful.

Unless you're extremely jaded, bring a handkerchief.

